{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_92","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,pathlib\np=pathlib.Path('exit-interview.json');v=json.loads(p.read_text());v['testingFeedback']=[\n'16 unique game, UI and integration issues found and fixed; test-harness false positives are excluded. Details and covering checks are in docs/validation.md.',\n'1 critical remote-seat input lock, reproduced after a long packet gap with advancing action counters; fixed. No unresolved critical issues.',\n'The exact exported HTML campaign driven through native keyboard actions: all 26 rescues, 2 lives left, 15400 points, bombs/refill/damage/recovery and all pursuit states exercised. Real Hub client/bridge campaigns also won with player and dedicated hosts.',\n'The initial generic export regex: it matched harmless interview text and .wave properties rather than runtime imports or audio files. It was replaced with targeted packaging checks and actual file:// request evidence.'\n];v['engineFeedback']=[\n'Native shaded pixel drawing, TileMap/Grid navigation, continuous rig timing, synthesized audio, standard controller-accessible screens and exact headless stepping form a coherent foundation.',\n'Yes. Keeping a GridMover direction queued in flight initially skipped enemy junction decisions. Input.feed simulates gestures, so real touch pointers were needed to test the invisible stick. Both assumptions were corrected.',\n'A deterministic simultaneous rescue simulation with passengers, reserved homes, team resources, pursuit and an authoritative shared-world network adapter.',\n'Combining buffered movement, immediate reversal, explicit device seats and snapshot reconciliation while preserving the native renderer and menu behavior.',\n'Added a hidden:true setting flag to the native Shell catalogue filter. Developer sliders still use native controls on explicit developer pages, while ordinary Settings and production Hub sessions do not expose them.',\n'A native simultaneous-seat arcade shell and a documented custom-creature rig base would reduce integration work.'\n];p.write_text(json.dumps(v,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
